# Button icon + text layout

Whenever a button (or button-like control) contains **both an icon and text**, wrap or style the contents so they lay out with flex. Do not leave icon and label as unstyled siblings.

## Required

Use flex alignment and a small gap:

- `inline-flex items-center gap-2` (or `gap-1.5` for compact buttons)
- Keep icon size consistent (`h-4 w-4` typical; `shrink-0` on the icon)

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — icon and text not flexed
<button type="button">
  <Plus className="h-4 w-4" />
  Add document type
</button>

// ✅ GOOD
<button
  type="button"
  className="inline-flex items-center gap-2"
>
  <Plus className="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
  Add document type
</button>
```

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — when using the shared Button component, flex the children
<Button variant="primary" size="md">
  <span className="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
    <Upload className="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
    Upload sample
  </span>
</Button>
```

## Also applies to

- Links styled as buttons
- Pill / chip action controls that mix icon + label
- Icon-after-text (e.g. “Next” + chevron): same `inline-flex items-center gap-2`
